  "id": "illumination-unit",
  "term": "illumination unit",
  "definition": "An illumination unit is the light source setup used to shine specific wavelengths into a fundus camera during retinal imaging. In this context, it was a custom LED system that delivered the two wavelengths needed for serial dual-wavelength retinal vessel oximetry.",
